// Agent is the seam between pack-target-host (the driver) and the process it runs on a managed host — the agent.
// The driver delivers the agent's binary to the host over SSH (or starts it locally), the agent listens on the
// host's loopback and the driver reaches it through the SSH connection (a direct-tcpip channel). Every call
// carries the token the driver started the agent with as the metadata pack-agent-token. The agent exits when
// its stdin closes — the SSH session's end is its lifetime's.
//
// The RPCs are the primitives an installation step on a classic host needs: run a command (a package manager,
// systemctl, sysctl, modprobe, the docker CLI — never a shell of the driver's), deliver and remove files, and
// serve the files of an OCI artifact over HTTP on the loopback (oci-proxy, for package repositories kept in a
// registry).

